# Payouts

The Payouts section explains how sellers receive their earnings from the Codexeron Marketplace.

All payouts are processed according to the current marketplace payment policy.

---

# Overview

Your earnings become available for payout after eligible sales have been processed.

The payout section allows you to:

- View your available balance
- Review payout history
- Monitor payout status
- Manage your payout information

---

# Supported Payment Method

Codexeron currently supports payouts via:

- USDT (Tether)

Additional payout methods may be introduced in future releases.

---

# Payout Request

When payout requests are available, sellers can request a payout from their available balance.

Before requesting a payout, ensure that:

- Your payout information is correct.
- Your available balance meets the minimum payout requirements (if applicable).
- Your account complies with marketplace policies.

---

# Payout Status

A payout request may have one of the following statuses:

| Status | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Pending | The payout request has been received and is awaiting review or processing. |
| Processing | The payout is currently being processed. |
| Completed | The payout has been successfully sent. |
| Failed | The payout could not be completed. |

---

# Payout History

Your payout history may include:

- Payout ID
- Request Date
- Payment Method
- Amount
- Status

Keeping track of your payout history helps with financial records and reporting.

---

# Payment Security

To help protect your earnings:

- Verify your payout wallet address before submitting a request.
- Never share your account credentials.
- Protect your account with a strong password.
- Enable Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) when available.

---

# Important Notes

Codexeron reserves the right to delay or suspend payouts if:

- Fraudulent activity is suspected.
- Marketplace policies have been violated.
- Additional verification is required.

---

# Best Practices

To ensure smooth payouts:

- Keep your account information up to date.
- Review your payout details carefully.
- Monitor your payout history.
- Contact support if you notice unexpected activity.

